        "y0": 0.14255808080808074,
        "x1": 0.9202075163398693,
        "y1": 0.18538383838383832
      },
      "text": "Next, we consider the downlink of data transmission where the BS applies a baseband precoder W ∈ CMt×Ms to transmit symbol s ∈ CMs×1, with E ssH = IM",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7978398692810458,
        "y0": 0.1727095959595959,
        "x1": 0.9201666666666668,
        "y1": 0.1841060606060606
      },
      "text": ". Furthermore, the",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7905849673202615,
        "y0": 0.17995959595959599,
        "x1": 0.7960375816993465,
        "y1": 0.1856148989898989
      },
      "text": "s",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5098006535947712,
        "y0": 0.18521464646464658,
        "x1": 0.9202091503267974,
        "y1": 0.2294090909090909
      },
      "text": "precoder satisﬁes W 2F ≤ pd and pd is the total transmit power at the BS. Thus the received signal at the user is obtained as",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5098006535947712,
        "y0": 0.23602020202020202,
        "x1": 0.9203627450980392,
        "y1": 0.2847992424242425
      },
      "text": "r = HeWs + nUE, (3) where nUE ∈ CMr×1 is the noise at the user with an average noise power of σUE2 , satisfying nUE ∼ CN 0M",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8317614379084968,
        "y0": 0.2683964646464647,
        "x1": 0.883779411764706,
        "y1": 0.2847992424242425
      },
      "text": ",σUE2 IM",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8988218954248365,
        "y0": 0.27089141414141416,
        "x1": 0.902890522875817,
        "y1": 0.28228787878787875
      },
      "text": ".",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8837222222222222,
        "y0": 0.2781426767676768,
        "x1": 0.8891846405228759,
        "y1": 0.2837967171717173
      },
      "text": "r",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8245081699346405,
        "y0": 0.2781426767676768,
        "x1": 0.8299689542483659,
        "y1": 0.2837967171717173
      },
      "text": "r",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5098006535947712,
        "y0": 0.2872550505050505,
        "x1": 0.9201470588235294,
        "y1": 0.31380303030303036
      },
      "text": "Meanwhile, we adopt the Rician channel in this paper. Speciﬁcally, the RIS-user channel can be expressed as",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "picture",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6431176470588236,
        "y0": 0.31986363636363635,
        "x1": 0.6929215686274509,
        "y1": 0.32046969696969696
      },
      "text": null,
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "picture",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7633137254901962,
        "y0": 0.3201666666666667,
        "x1": 0.8131176470588235,
        "y1": 0.3207727272727273
      },
      "text": null,
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "caption",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6450980392156863,
        "y0": 0.3216262626262626,
        "x1": 0.6906895424836601,
        "y1": 0.3522020202020202
      },
      "text": "Fr Fr + 1",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "caption",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7652941176470588,
        "y0": 0.3216262626262626,
        "x1": 0.8110800653594771,
        "y1": 0.3522020202020202
      },
      "text": "1 Fr + 1",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "picture",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5948823529411764,
        "y0": 0.32759090909090904,
        "x1": 0.6113529411764707,
        "y1": 0.32819696969696976
      },
      "text": null,
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6927450980392157,
        "y0": 0.3283358585858587,
        "x1": 0.7434330065359477,
        "y1": 0.34477777777777774
      },
      "text": "HLoSr +",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8129411764705882,
        "y0": 0.3283358585858587,
        "x1": 0.920125816993464,
        "y1": 0.34477777777777774
      },
      "text": "HNLoSr , (4)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "caption",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5349003267973856,
        "y0": 0.33011111111111113,
        "x1": 0.6101568627450981,
        "y1": 0.34356565656565663
      },
      "text": "Hr = βr",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "picture",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.645078431372549,
        "y0": 0.3360757575757576,
        "x1": 0.6909607843137254,
        "y1": 0.3366818181818182
      },
      "text": null,
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "picture",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7652745098039216,
        "y0": 0.3360757575757576,
        "x1": 0.811156862745098,
        "y1": 0.3366818181818182
      },
      "text": null,
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5098039215686274,
        "y0": 0.3582929292929292,
        "x1": 0.92034477124183,
        "y1": 0.46432323232323236
      },
      "text": "where βr and Fr are the path loss and the Rician factor of RIS-user channel, respectively; HLoSr ∈ CMr×N and HNLoSr ∈ CMr×N represent the line-of-sight (LoS) and the non-line-of-sight (NLoS) components of the RIS-user channel, respectively. The element on the mrth row and the nth column of the NLoS matrix is modeled by Rayleigh fading, which follows HNLoSr m",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5098039215686274,
        "y0": 0.448584595959596,
        "x1": 0.9199313725490197,
        "y1": 0.4762272727272727
      },
      "text": "r,n ∼ CN (0,1). Similarly, the BS-user channel and BS-RIS channel can be modeled by using (4).",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5098039215686274,
        "y0": 0.4811944444444445,
        "x1": 0.9204330065359476,
        "y1": 0.6758724747474747
      },
      "text": "Moreover, we consider a uniform linear array (ULA) at the BS, a ULA at the user, and a uniform planar array (UPA) at the RIS. Let aBS (δ) ∈ CMt×1, aUE (δ) ∈ CMr×1 and aR (ζ,γ) ∈ CN×1 denote the steering vector of the BS, the user and the RIS, respectively. Speciﬁcally, the mtth entry of aBS is denoted as ej2λπ(mt−1)dBS sin(δ),mt = 1,2,··· ,Mt, where dBS denotes the element spacing of the BS, λ denotes the signal wavelength, and δ ∈ [−π/2,π/2) denotes the angle of departure (AoD) or the angle of arrival (AoA). Similarly, the mrth entry of aUE is denoted as ej2λπ(mr−1)dUE sin(δ),mr = 1,2,··· ,Mr, where dUE denotes the element spacing of the user. The nth entry of aR is denoted as ej2πd",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "picture",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7599803921568627,
        "y0": 0.5583484848484848,
        "x1": 0.7727254901960785,
        "y1": 0.5588030303030302
      },
      "text": null,
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "picture",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5252745098039217,
        "y0": 0.6338030303030302,
        "x1": 0.5380196078431372,
        "y1": 0.6342575757575757
      },
      "text": null,
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5098022875816994,
        "y0": 0.6585959595959596,
        "x1": 0.9201683006535948,
        "y1": 0.7357727272727272
      },
      "text": "R sin(γ)[⌊nN−x1⌋sin(ζ)+((n−1)−⌊nN−x1⌋Nx) cos(ζ)]/λ,n = 1,2,··· ,N, where dR denotes the element spacing of the RIS. Nx is the number of elements deployed at each row of the RIS. ζ ∈ [0,π) and γ ∈ [−π/2,π/2) denote the azimuth and elevation AoA/AoD, respectively. Thus, the LoS component of the",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "picture",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6278235294117647,
        "y0": 0.6647121212121212,
        "x1": 0.6493921568627451,
        "y1": 0.6651666666666667
      },
      "text": null,
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "picture",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7603725490196078,
        "y0": 0.6647121212121212,
        "x1": 0.7819411764705883,
        "y1": 0.6651666666666667
      },
      "text": null,
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5098022875816994,
        "y0": 0.7352146464646465,
        "x1": 0.9201699346405229,
        "y1": 0.8607727272727272
      },
      "text": "Ht, Hr and Hd are given by aR ζtAoA,γtAoA aBS δtAoD H, aUE δrAoA aR ζrAoD,γrAoD H and aUE δdAoA aBS δdAoD H, respectively, where δtAoD, ζtAoA and γtAoA represent the AoD, the azimuth and elevation AoA from the BS to the RIS, respectively; δrAoA, ζrAoD and γrAoD represent the AoA, the azimuth and elevation AoD from the RIS to the user, respectively; δdAoA and δdAoD represent the AoA and the AoD from the BS to the user, respectively.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5098039215686274,
        "y0": 0.865739898989899,
        "x1": 0.9206879084967321,
        "y1": 0.9072878787878788
      },
      "text": "In the next section, unlike traditional passive beamforming and codebook schemes, the proposed scheme maximizes the channel capacity of the point-to-point MIMO systems by",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    }
